Engine: the engine's own window hidden from the start (open fix 41).

STATUS: NOT APPLIED — written and proved by work order 182 (Part 2),
parked for Data (doc/briefs/182-parked-for-data.md, item 1). No engine
patch may be applied in that order.

PROOF (work order 182, 27 September 2026): in a scratch clone of
orionlayer-local 2097b0c6 (never on orionlayer-local itself) this file
applied with `patch -p1 --dry-run` and `patch -p1`, no offset, no fuzz,
and the applied tree equals the scratch commit; the scratch engine was
built in full with the linux-debug preset (ORION2RE_EXT=ON) — no error —
and a control, the same file with `ext::g_hide_window` misspelt
`ext::g_hide_windw` in platform.cpp, was refused by the compiler. The
scratch engine then ran on the virtual display and on a real session:
see the entry, doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md 41.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch (after fix 40):

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_engine_window_hidden.patch

then rebuild. It comes back off with `patch -R -p1` and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    platform.cpp creates the window with SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN and shows it
    at the end of its setup unless ext::g_hide_window is set
    (platform.cpp:1406-1408). ext::Init() sets that flag — but only from
    mox2.cpp:382, after the platform layer has run, so in every
    ORION2RE_EXT build the window is shown first (decision 39's
    correction). The header already says what the flag is for: "suppress
    SDL_ShowWindow (headless mode)". This decides it before the show.

    A hidden window is never drawn by a compositor, and a VSync present
    to a window nobody draws can wait for ever (open fix 31). So a hidden
    window presents without VSync, whatever ORION2RE_NO_VSYNC says.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 9b293a82..88c157cd 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 
 namespace ext {
 
-bool g_hide_window = false;
+bool g_hide_window = true;  // OrionLayer, open fix 41. Hidden before the window is first shown, not after (platform.cpp).
 int16_t g_pending_field = 0;
 int16_t g_activated_input = 0;
 bool g_injected_mouse_pending = false;
diff --git a/src/game/platform.cpp b/src/game/platform.cpp
index 399f9589..3f943781 100644
--- a/src/game/platform.cpp
+++ b/src/game/platform.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,10 @@ namespace platform {
 		// (video::Submit_Palette_, video::Publish_Off_Page_): the start
 		// hangs in its first logo frames. Unattended runs set this.
 		int Present_VSync_Interval_() {
+			// OrionLayer, open fix 41. A hidden window is never drawn, so it never presents with VSync.
+			if (ext::g_hide_window) {
+				return 0;
+			}
 			const char* value = SDL_getenv("ORION2RE_NO_VSYNC");
 			return (value != nullptr && value[0] != '\0' && value[0] != '0') ? 0 : 1;
 		}
